<title>LEBANON: Banque Beyrouth pour le Commerce 96' profits up.</title>
<headline>Banque Beyrouth pour le Commerce 96' profits up.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banque Beyrouth pour le Commerce posted a 190 percent rise in 1996 net profits, according to its balance sheet published in Lebanese newspapers on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Assets grew by 36.4 percent, customer deposits climbed 31.2 percent and loans and credits increased by 21.2 percent.</p>
<p>It published the following results in billions of Lebanese pounds:</p>
<p>				1996		    1995</p>
<p>    Profits		 6.34		    2.18</p>
<p>    Assets	     788.421		  577.860</p>
<p>    Deposits	   644.523		  490.942</p>
<p>Loans &amp;</p>
<p>    Credits	    190.251		  156.980</p>
<p>The bank has 17 branches in Lebanon with 354 employees.</p>
<p>($1 = 1,538 Lebanese pounds)</p>
<p>-- Beirut editorial (9611) - 602057 745308 745309</p>
</text>
